## The Hero: Cholesterol and Nutrients

It’s not just about removing the bad stuff; it’s about adding the good stuff. The Carnivore Diet is incredibly nutrient-dense in ways that specifically love on your skin.

### 1. Cholesterol is Cool

Despite the bad PR it got in the 90s, cholesterol is a vital building block for every cell in your body. It provides structural integrity to cell membranes. More importantly, your body uses cholesterol in the skin to **synthesize Vitamin D** from sunlight.

### 2. The Nutrient Army

Steak isn't just protein; it's a multivitamin.

* **Zinc:** Vital for skin healing and protection.
* **Selenium:** Helps reduce oxidative stress.
* **Glycine:** Found in collagen (connective tissue/bones), this amino acid helps repair tissue damage.

> **Fun Fact:** Tallow (rendered beef fat) is biologically very similar to human skin oil. That’s why so many carnivores ditch the expensive moisturizers and just use whipped tallow on their face!

